A||N||3||rhauser||AC Compressor Top Bolt||||1||
Z||000000||rhauser||11-16-2001||09:19 PM||||I need to get a belt on my AC compressor (mysteriously missing when I bought it).  I can loosen the lower bolt but the top is holding it firm, is there a trick to getting to it?<P>Also, is there any way to test the functionality of the compressor before I waste the time of putting a belt on it?<P>Thanks in advance,<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||FIERO1985||11-16-2001||11:27 PM||||ok, usually the top bolt is a *****  but use a long extension and I universal swivel I thought the bolt was a 15mm but not sure. That is how I took My compressor off. It locked up. Good way to test a compressor is like testing a front end for bad wheel bearings and/or balljoints and other things. Just spin the pulley(clutch) she if it wobbles side to side or have excessive play in it. Really I hate the ac on fieros Take it off and roll windows down.<P>Oh well good luck<BR>Dan<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||11-17-2001||01:04 AM||||Yes, the top bolts are 15mm - one through the bracket into the compressor and one through the bracket and compressor into a nut. If you loosen the bottom bolt you can use a large screwdriver or small pry bar in the slotted holes in the lower a/c bracket to maneuver the compressor back and forth - much easier than trying to take the top bolts loose!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||11-17-2001||12:42 PM||||The first test I would do is to have some one turn on the a/c with the low press switch plug(located in the front compartment, near the drier) jumped. This will allow the clutch coil to energize, even if the system is low on freon. You can see it when it engages, or at least feel it with your hand. Then rotate the compressor pulley to see if it is locked up or not. Then check for play as suggested above. Naturally, you do this with the key on but engine not running.||||reg||1
